My approach (two pointer approach):-
1.Initialise two pointers one from i = 0 and one from i + 1 and product will update if product is greater than max product 
2.Mistake: I ignored the error where i is at last index where j goes beyond the size so it doesn't process at last index properly.So try to wrap the inner loop inside an if(i!=lastIndex) block such that this error is rectified 
3.return the max product.

Time complexity: O(N²)
Space complexity: O(N)

My code:-
int maxProduct(vector<int>& nums) {
         int product = nums[0];
         int max_product = nums[0];
        for(int i = 0;i<nums.size();i++){
            product = nums[i];
            if(i!= nums.size() -1){
            for(int j = i+1;j<nums.size();j++){
                product = product * nums[j];
                if(product > max_product)
                max_product = product;
            }
            }
            if(nums[i]>max_product){
                max_product = nums[i];
            }
        }
        return max_product;
    }